+++ b/docs/catalog-ingestion/PROVIDER_NEUTRAL_ARCHITECTURE.md
@@ -74,3 +74,11 @@ Synthetic test-only review states exercise gates; imports themselves do not crea
 Before a licensed BGG adapter: secure and review the commercial agreement; define server-side authorization and permitted fields, rate limits, retention, and audit controls; document metadata rights separately from image display, caching, transformation, and attribution rights; then build an adapter and test it only with authorized access. If denied, publisher-authorized, suitably licensed open, and GameFinder-curated providers remain viable through the same candidate contract.
 
 Before production ingestion, promote a separately reviewed staging schema through versioned migrations, validate durability on the deployed PostgreSQL configuration, and add trusted server-side authorization, permission-expiry/revocation enforcement, human review tooling, observability, and rollback. Before permanent-ID migration, separately reconcile legacy identities and aliases, resolve known collisions, map every Vault/history/score reference, and test a reviewed reversible migration. Production publication additionally requires approved identity, verified hard-filter facts with evidence, cleared metadata rights, separately approved eligible artwork, human review, owner approval, and an explicit publication/rollback process.
+
+## Phase 03 collection import planning and validation hardening
+
+The internal collection preview accepts bounded provider-namespaced claims and independently reviewed permanent identities. It reports invalid, unresolved, ambiguous, review-required, already-owned, duplicate and eligible records without writing user data. An exact normalized title is a consistency check, not identity evidence. Verified external IDs with unresolved conflicts are not eligible. The confirmation planner recomputes eligibility and capacity from current trusted inputs, rejects stale or fabricated selections, preserves existing ownership, and supports idempotent replay. It does not truncate an oversized collection or perform persistence. Existing legacy IDs are not automatically reconciled to permanent IDs; the planner is a future permanent-identity interface, not an adapter for the current Vault.
+
+Neither function is exposed as a route or server endpoint. Before activation, require licensed provider access, authenticated account ownership, trusted server-side identity and entitlement checks, approved permanent-ID compatibility, transactional additive writes with concurrency checks, and an explicit user confirmation flow. No BGG access, user-facing import, global publication or identity migration is enabled by this checkpoint.
+
+Identity resolution now rejects unresolved conflicts even when an alias is verified. Metadata and artwork validation reject invalid evaluation dates and future-dated reviews, require identified reviewers and chronological approvals, and published snapshots reject reused provider source records. These are validation controls, not proof that supplied approval data came from a trusted actor.
